Make xmllintMain reset its statics on every call.

xmllint is written as a program that runs once and exits: its options and its
exit status live in file-scope statics. This build keeps one Emscripten
instance alive and calls main once per document, so those statics carry over —
after a document fails, every later one is reported as failing too, while the
output still says it validates.

xmllint.c already resets all of it, guarded by XMLLINT_FUZZ, because libxml2's
own fuzzer drives xmllintMain in a loop the same way. That flag cannot be used
here: it also moves diagnostics from stderr to stdout, where they would be
indistinguishable from --format output, and it drops the no-net entity loader
for --nonet. So the reset gets a guard of its own.

--- a/xmllint.c
+++ b/xmllint.c
@@ -3128,7 +3128,11 @@ xmllintMain(int argc, const char **argv) {
     int nocatalogs = 0;
 #endif
 
-#ifdef XMLLINT_FUZZ
+/* Reset every static this program holds, so that a second call to xmllintMain
+   in the same process starts clean. XMLLINT_FUZZ enables it for the fuzzer,
+   which also wants diagnostics on stdout and its own main(); a host that keeps
+   one instance alive across documents wants only the reset. */
+#if defined(XMLLINT_FUZZ) || defined(XMLLINT_REENTRANT)
 #ifdef LIBXML_DEBUG_ENABLED
     shell = 0;
     debugent = 0;
